# Public shop details. They are inlined when the site is built, because product
# pages are prerendered and share the header with the rest of the site.
# Leave a variable unset to hide that panel. Do not commit real values.
# PUBLIC_SHOP_NAME changes the logo, page titles, and the name on a receipt.
# Unset, the name is Lahore Silicon.

# PUBLIC_SHOP_NAME=
# PUBLIC_SHOP_PHONE=
# PUBLIC_RAAST_ID=
# PUBLIC_RAAST_ACCOUNT_NAME=
# PUBLIC_RAAST_BANK=
# PUBLIC_JAZZCASH_NUMBER=
# PUBLIC_SADAPAY_NUMBER=
# PUBLIC_BANK_NAME=
# PUBLIC_BANK_ACCOUNT_TITLE=
# PUBLIC_BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER=
# PUBLIC_BANK_IBAN=

# Turnstile. Checkout refuses an order the server cannot verify.
# Local astro dev can use Cloudflare's published test keys (they always pass).
# Dummy siteverify reports hostname example.com and does not return an action.
#   PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES=example.com
# Production: `wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET`, and set PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY
# to the real sitekey. Hostnames ship as the wrangler var lahoresilicon.com.
# Do not deploy the test secret, and do not add localhost to that allowlist.
# PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=
# TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES=
